    },
    {
      "id": "claim_66a10287380d4c26bca37f7e251e6b2d",
      "statement": "OfflineCA wraps authority.New from smallstep/certificates over a locally supplied ca.json (--ca-config), turning the CA server's signing logic into an in-process client; it is a singleton (offlineInstance) because double initialization can be impossible due to locks such as badgerDB's, so NewOfflineCA returns the existing instance on repeat calls.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L30-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09bae3f7915c32fcb70708e0aff3c7be825b25a8b193ec552f2ceb68650ae936:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L36-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f241e3dab29b41e4b18ec3076f652143658897611262a8037d1d57a7f6cd4392:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b56ebead6a72433f9417c166a3cbf077",
      "statement": "Offline token generation mirrors the online NewTokenFlow but sources root and audience from ca.json (Audience maps token types to https://<first-DNS>/<endpoint> paths), uses provisioners from the config without a network call, and takes the JWK provisioner's encryptedKey directly from ca.json where the online path fetches it from the CA; it dispatches to the same per-provisioner generators including OIDC and the ACME/SCEP errors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L141-L158",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c6829dabc1878cd366c30e3a437db1510e4af5edb959edbb382f1d2bf8cd798:"
