    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec95cdcd83074b3f829b3824356922d9",
      "statement": "Every OfflineCA operation is a wrapper over the authority API — Sign authorizes the OTT then calls authority.SignWithContext, Renew parses the peer certificate from the transport and calls authority.Renew, Revoke authorizes via OTT or the mTLS client certificate, Rekey uses authority.Rekey, and SSH methods wrap their authority counterparts — returning responses shaped exactly like the online API (ServerPEM, CaPEM, CertChainPEM) so callers cannot distinguish modes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L175-L181",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b60c6b9dfc1381f8d4781f849453315fe400c284c6e3f7891fcdc4ecec09f2e8:"
