    {
      "id": "claim_088040961724442285578a4aa891d7e0",
      "statement": "CreateSignRequest generates the key from --kty/--curve/--size and builds the CSR by token type: JWK-like tokens take the subject from the token payload; AWS/GCP/Azure identity tokens derive default SANs from the instance identity document (private IP and internal hostname, GCP internal DNS names, Azure resource name) appending the CLI subject unless DisableCustomSANs is set; OIDC without SANs and subject==email yields CN=token subject with email and iss#sub URI SANs; K8sSA ignores the token subject because those tokens are multi-use.",
      "evidence": [
